{"title": "Vent", "pageid": 47941, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Vent", "categories": ["Environmental objects", "Traps"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:GasVentBasic.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/e/e0/GasVentBasic.png/150px-GasVentBasic.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/e/e0/GasVentBasic.png/225px-GasVentBasic.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/e/e0/GasVentBasic.png/300px-GasVentBasic.png.webp 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/e/e0/GasVentBasic.png/150px-GasVentBasic.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/e/e0/GasVentBasic.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption>Most common Vent Trap.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>A <b>Vent</b> is a common type of a <a href=\"/wiki/Trap\" title=\"Trap\">Trap</a> that might be encountered almost in every location of the game.\n</p><p>A Vent is a mechanism hidden within the ground. It is implied to cause continuous damage to a trespasser who proceeds into locations where their presence is obviously unwanted.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Involvement\">Involvement</span></h2>\n<p>Vents encountered throughout the game may generally come in either of two types:\n</p>\n<ul><li><i>Triggerable Vent.</i> Triggerable Vents work upon stepping on them (or close to them), or upon interacting with trigger element nearby, as long as the trap is not disarmed. The effect of triggering this kind of Vents is various, too, but most common ones are spilling around <a href=\"/wiki/Simple_Toxin_(surface)\" title=\"Simple Toxin (surface)\">toxin</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Grease_(surface)\" title=\"Grease (surface)\">grease</a> or issuing <a href=\"/wiki/Poison_Cloud\" title=\"Poison Cloud\">Poison Cloud</a>.</li>\n<li><i>Constantly issuing Vent.</i> Constantly issuing Vents produce in the surrounding area clouds of various damaging substances, for example, hot steam or poisonous gas. Often combined with any fire-issuing traps, these vents might have the effect of a fuel-air explosion if triggered together.</li></ul>\n<p>A Vent can be disarmed with the help of <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Sleight_of_Hand\" title=\"Sleight of Hand\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png/25px-Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png/38px-Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png/50px-Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Sleight of Hand\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png/25px-Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Sleight_of_Hand\" title=\"Sleight of Hand\">Sleight of Hand</a> skill, but the interacting party member must have a <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit\" title=\"Trap Disarm Toolkit\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png/40px-Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit\" title=\"Trap Disarm Toolkit\">Trap Disarm Toolkit</a> in their inventory. Minimal requirement is a <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/30px-D20.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/40px-D20.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"DC&nbsp;10 Sleight of Hand Check\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/1/13/D20.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> DC&nbsp;10 <a href=\"/wiki/Sleight_of_Hand\" title=\"Sleight of Hand\">Sleight of Hand</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Ability_check\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ability check\">Check</a> roll, but the <a href=\"/wiki/Difficulty_Class\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Difficulty Class\">Difficulty Class</a> may vary depending on circumstances.\n</p><p>Apart from disarming, there is another way to stop the harmful effect of a <i>constantly issuing</i> Vent. To do this, a party member must place (or throw) on-top the Vent any object massive enough to \"fother the leak\". Doing so will remove at once the harmful cloud from the space above the trap, but it is actually a half-way measure. Removing placed/thrown object without disarming the trap first will lead to activating the Vent anew.\nBesides, to do this, any party member must first make a successful <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Perception\" title=\"Perception\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/92/Perception_Icon.png/25px-Perception_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/9/92/Perception_Icon.png/38px-Perception_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/9/92/Perception_Icon.png/50px-Perception_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Perception\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/9/92/Perception_Icon.png/25px-Perception_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/9/92/Perception_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Perception\" title=\"Perception\">Perception</a> roll to detect the exact place of the issuing aperture, otherwise it won't be possible to interact with it. \n</p><p>After disarming, a Vent will be pictured almost same as a newly spotted one, but if it was previously triggered, the depiction of its effect will disappear. For example, part of the floor around toxin-spilling vent will change to a clear one after disarming the trap.\n</p><p>Throughout <i>Baldur's Gate 3</i>, Vents are the type of <a href=\"/wiki/Trap\" title=\"Trap\">Traps</a> that features the biggest amount of variations accordingly to the place where they are planted. Some of these kinds cannot be encountered anywhere else in the game.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span></h3>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-nolines center\" style=\"max-width: 954px;margin:0 auto;\">\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:GasVentNox.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"A Vent issuing Noxious Fumes (Overgrown Tunnel).\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/5/5f/GasVentNox.png/150px-GasVentNox.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/5/5f/GasVentNox.png/225px-GasVentNox.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/5/5f/GasVentNox.png/300px-GasVentNox.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"A Vent issuing Noxious Fumes (Overgrown Tunnel).\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/5/5f/GasVentNox.png/150px-GasVentNox.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/5/5f/GasVentNox.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">A Vent issuing Noxious Fumes (Overgrown Tunnel).</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:GasVentWyrm.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"A Stunner Vent (Rooftop of the Wyrm's Rock Fortress).\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/c/c4/GasVentWyrm.png/150px-GasVentWyrm.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/c/c4/GasVentWyrm.png/225px-GasVentWyrm.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/c/c4/GasVentWyrm.png/300px-GasVentWyrm.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"A Stunner Vent (Rooftop of the Wyrm's Rock Fortress).\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/c/c4/GasVentWyrm.png/150px-GasVentWyrm.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/c/c4/GasVentWyrm.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">A Stunner Vent (Rooftop of the Wyrm's Rock Fortress).</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:VoidVent.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"A Vent issuing a Void Cloud (Gauntlet of Shar).\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/16/VoidVent.png/150px-VoidVent.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/16/VoidVent.png/225px-VoidVent.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/16/VoidVent.png/300px-VoidVent.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"A Vent issuing a Void Cloud (Gauntlet of Shar).\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/16/VoidVent.png/150px-VoidVent.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/1/16/VoidVent.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">A Vent issuing a Void Cloud (Gauntlet of Shar).</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:SanguineVent.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"A Sanguine Vent issues puddles of Unstable Blood (Undercity Ruins).\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/f/f6/SanguineVent.png/150px-SanguineVent.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/f/f6/SanguineVent.png/225px-SanguineVent.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/f/f6/SanguineVent.png/300px-SanguineVent.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"A Sanguine Vent issues puddles of Unstable Blood (Undercity Ruins).\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/f/f6/SanguineVent.png/150px-SanguineVent.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/f/f6/SanguineVent.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">A Sanguine Vent issues puddles of Unstable Blood (Undercity Ruins).</div>\n\t\t</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714194818\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.030 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 934/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 6653/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 1346/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 19/200\nExpensive parser function count: 0/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3889/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/1000\nLua time usage: 0.009/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 731214/52428800 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   20.766      1 -total\n 56.45%   11.722    